WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.141
(ding)

00:00:02.061 --> 00:00:04.346
- I have absolutely no idea what Arak is.

00:00:04.346 --> 00:00:05.683
- To be honest, when I first heard

00:00:05.683 --> 00:00:07.383
the name of it, I thought of the country.

00:00:07.383 --> 00:00:11.896
(Middle Eastern music)

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.350
I'm told that this is
like a major, iconic drink

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:22.077
in a lot of Middle Eastern countries.

00:00:22.077 --> 00:00:23.319
- [Man] This is clear.
- [Woman] Yeah.

00:00:23.319 --> 00:00:25.133
- [Man] I don't like that,
it reminds me of moonshine.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.563
- 50% alcohol!

00:00:26.563 --> 00:00:27.650
- That's a really little bottle

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.517
to contain 27 drinks.

00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:30.604
- Is that, that's a lot.

00:00:30.604 --> 00:00:32.359
- So, for Caitlin, someone
who doesn't drink often,

00:00:32.359 --> 00:00:33.752
this is gonna suck.

00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:35.229
- Smells like black licorice.

00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:37.625
- We go one-third Arak
and then two-thirds water.

00:00:37.625 --> 00:00:39.353
- Like, I don't get the whole water thing.

00:00:39.353 --> 00:00:41.526
Like, can you not just drink it straight?

00:00:42.546 --> 00:00:44.444
Whoa, it's like a weird --

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.503
- Is that milk?

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:46.930
- You know dishwashing water?

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:48.170
- I don't like that, it makes me feel

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.546
like there's something going on in there.

00:00:50.546 --> 00:00:52.691
- All right, cheers, bottoms up.

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:55.715
- [Caitlin] Oh, it's fine!
- [Man] Oh, no,

00:00:55.715 --> 00:00:56.665
it's quite nice!

00:00:56.665 --> 00:00:58.615
- Ugh, it gets you.

00:00:58.615 --> 00:01:01.346
- The first initial taste is
like really (bleep) strong

00:01:01.346 --> 00:01:02.600
and then it's great.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.968
- It kind of reminds me
of like an ouzo or grappa.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:06.752
- I would say that's straight up Galliano.

00:01:06.752 --> 00:01:08.563
- It's definitely an
I'm-getting-drunk drink.

00:01:08.563 --> 00:01:10.513
- You can definitely
taste the alcohol in this,

00:01:10.513 --> 00:01:12.993
but it's not overpowering,
which doesn't really make sense,

00:01:12.993 --> 00:01:15.250
'cause there's about 50 drinks in that.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:16.365
- That totally makes sense now

00:01:16.365 --> 00:01:17.563
why we had to add water.

00:01:17.563 --> 00:01:18.538
- This can be dangerous.

00:01:18.538 --> 00:01:19.903
- Doesn't even feel alcoholic.

00:01:19.903 --> 00:01:22.328
It feels like cordial that's
meant to taste like licorice.

00:01:22.328 --> 00:01:26.006
- A long, never-ending shot of
I want to go home now please.

00:01:26.006 --> 00:01:27.594
- I came in thinking I'll be drinking

00:01:27.594 --> 00:01:30.826
the most ghastly drink
ever, but it was great!

00:01:30.826 --> 00:01:32.470
- I don't think that I'd be bringing

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:35.507
this out every weekend, not at all.

00:01:35.507 --> 00:01:36.650
- I'm feelin' a buzz.

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:38.934
- This is the prime drink you can

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:40.355
sneak into a music festival.

00:01:40.355 --> 00:01:42.640
- Yeah, just say it's like fancy water.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.591
- This is probably up there with

00:01:44.591 --> 00:01:46.458
one of the strongest drinks I've ever had.

00:01:46.458 --> 00:01:47.879
- This right here is everything I want

00:01:47.879 --> 00:01:49.606
in a drink: it's easy to go down,

00:01:49.606 --> 00:01:52.170
it's alcoholic as hell,
and it's refreshing.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:54.928
Great job, guys, love it.

00:01:54.928 --> 00:01:56.349
- So they drink this in the Middle East.

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.102
- Yes.

00:01:57.102 --> 00:01:58.774
- In countries like Iraq.

00:01:58.774 --> 00:02:00.242
- Yup.

00:02:00.242 --> 00:02:02.314
(laughter)

00:02:02.314 --> 00:02:03.102
- I tricked him.

00:02:03.102 --> 00:02:04.412
(laughter)

00:02:04.412 --> 00:02:05.145
I love this.

00:02:05.145 --> 00:02:06.879
- [Man in white] It's great.
- [Man in blue] I would

00:02:06.879 --> 00:02:07.663
straight up love this.

